---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout description="A warm place to log learning, plan homeschool days, keep their work, read the Bible, and connect with the families in your village. In development for mobile.">
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line" aria-hidden="true"></span> A LITTLE LIGHT FOR THE JOURNEY</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Your homeschool<br /> <em>village.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">For the learning.<br /> And the life around it.</p>
      <p class="hero-description">Log learning, plan your days, keep their work, and connect with the families walking alongside you.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/pilot/">Join the pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/features/">Get to know the app <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <p class="release-note">A free pilot on iPhone and iPad through TestFlight. Coming soon to the App Store.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-art">
      <img src="/art/village.webp" alt="An illustrated family and their neighbours walking along a winding path between welcoming homes." width="1600" height="1200" fetchpriority="high" />
      <figcaption><span class="caption-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span> EVERY FAMILY WALKS ITS OWN WAY. <span>YOU CAN WALK TOGETHER.</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="intro-section wrap" aria-labelledby="little-things">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE EVERYDAY, HELD TOGETHER</p>
    <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="little-things">The little things add up<br /> to a <em>meaningful year.</em></h2><p>A reading lesson. An art project. A day with friends. Along the Way brings the plans, records, and people of your homeschool into one place.</p></div>
    <div class="chapter-grid">
      <a class="chapter" href="/features/#learning-time"><span class="chapter-number">01 / RECORD</span><h3>See the learning<br /> in your days.</h3><p>Log time by subject, keep lesson notes, and see each child’s progress.</p><span class="text-link">Learning &amp; records <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
      <a class="chapter" href="/features/#day-planner"><span class="chapter-number">02 / MAKE ROOM</span><h3>A little structure.<br /> Room for life.</h3><p>Plan a day for everyone or one child. Mark a lesson done and record its time.</p><span class="text-link">Planning &amp; daily log <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
      <a class="chapter" href="/features/#your-village"><span class="chapter-number">03 / CONNECT</span><h3>Good company<br /> along the way.</h3><p>Connect with other homeschool families and share photos with your village.</p><span class="text-link">Family &amp; village <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="learning-section" aria-labelledby="work-worth-keeping">
    <div class="wrap split-section">
      <div class="art-frame"><img src="/art/learning.webp" alt="A faceless illustrated parent and child reading an open book beside a lit clay lamp." width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" /></div>
      <div class="section-copy"><p class="eyebrow">MORE THAN A NUMBER</p><h2 id="work-worth-keeping">Their work.<br /> <em>Your memories.</em></h2><p>Some days are worth keeping in more than a time log. Save a child’s artwork and projects in Keepsakes, your family’s private archive.</p><p>Add dates, titles, and notes so you can remember the learning behind the work.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/#keepsakes">A place for their keepsakes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="family-wall wrap" aria-labelledby="family-wall-title">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">A VILLAGE, WITH BOUNDARIES</p><h2 id="family-wall-title">Your family’s records<br /> stay with <em>your family.</em></h2></div>
    <div><p>Your village is for connection. Your children’s learning records, keepsakes, and Bible reading progress stay inside your family.</p><p>Photos you choose to share with your village are separate from those records. The app adds no child-name fields, tags, captions, or links to a child’s record.</p><a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Read the privacy policy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="faith-section" aria-labelledby="faith-title">
    <div class="wrap split-section">
      <div class="section-copy"><p class="eyebrow">FAITH IN THE EVERYDAY</p><h2 id="faith-title">A little time<br /> <em>in the Word.</em></h2><p>Open the built-in Bible, read together or for a child, and mark chapters as read. Choose the Berean Standard Bible or King James Version.</p><p>The reader is optional. Switch it on in Settings when it belongs in your family’s day.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/#bible-reading">Bible &amp; reading progress <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="art-frame"><img src="/art/bible-reading.webp" alt="An illustrated open Bible, a lamp, and a calendar with three reading days checked, beside a path toward sunrise." width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="verse-section wrap" aria-label="A verse for the journey"><span class="small-sun" aria-hidden="true">◒</span><blockquote>“Your word is a lamp to my feet<br /> and a light to my path.”</blockquote><p>PSALM 119:105 · BEREAN STANDARD BIBLE (BSB)</p></section>
  <section class="closing-section wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">COME WALK WITH US</p><h2>A place for your<br /> <em>homeschool days.</em></h2></div><div><p>Take a closer look at the tools, the family boundaries, and the village at the heart of Along the Way.</p><a class="button" href="/pilot/">Join the pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="release-note">Free on iPhone and iPad through TestFlight. Coming soon to the App Store.</p></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
